    {
      "evidence_id": "tei:abstract",
      "source": "grobid_tei",
      "field": "abstract",
      "raw_text": "We consider the map χ : F n 2 → F n 2 for n odd given by y = χ(x) with yi = xi + xi+2(1 + xi+1), where the indices are computed modulo n. We suggest a generalization of the map χ which we call generalized χ-maps. We show that these maps form an Abelian group which is isomorphic to the group of units in F2[X]/(X (n+1)/2). Using this isomorphism we easily obtain closed-form expressions for iterates of χ and explain their properties."
    },
