    {
      "evidence_id": "pdfplumber:abstract",
      "source": "pdf_layout",
      "field": "abstract",
      "raw_text": "We consider the map χ : Fn 2 → Fn 2 for n odd given by y = χ(x)w i t hyi = xi + xi+2(1 + xi+1), where the indices are com- puted modulo n. We suggest a generalization of the map χ which we call generalized χ-maps. We show that these maps form an Abelian group which is isomorphic to the group of units in F2[X]/(X(n+1)/2). Using this isomorphism we easily obtain closed-form expressions for iterates of χ and explain their properties.",
      "extractor": "pdfplumber_section_boundary"
